# UI, styling and accessibility

- Styling: plain CSS. Design tokens (color, spacing, radius, type scale) are CSS custom properties in `apps/web/src/lib/styles/tokens.css`; components use Svelte's scoped `<style>` and reference tokens only. No CSS framework, no inline color literals in components.
- Themes: light and dark from `prefers-color-scheme`, with a manual override stored in settings. Every token has both values.
- Target **WCAG 2.2 AA**:
  - Every interactive element is reachable and usable by keyboard, with a visible focus style.
  - Use native elements (`<button>`, `<select>`, `<dialog>`, `<table>`) before ARIA. Never put click handlers on `<div>`s.
  - Form fields have `<label>`s; validation errors are announced and tied to their field with `aria-describedby`.
  - Long-running work (simulations) reports progress in an `aria-live="polite"` region.
  - Color is never the only signal for side, status or result.
  - Every chart has a "show as table" toggle with the same numbers.
  - The grid canvas has a synchronized text event log as its accessible alternative, and full keyboard control (cell cursor with arrow keys, Enter, Escape).
  - **Single-workspace focus management:** with no page navigations to do it for you, move focus into a panel, drawer or dialog when it opens, return it to the control that opened it when it closes, and announce mode changes (Build, Play, Simulate, Review) in an `aria-live` region. Update `document.title` on mode change.
- **AI reasoning view** (Settings → "Show AI reasoning", off by default): each AI turn's "Why?" control is a `<button aria-expanded>` that reveals a real `<table>` of ranked options with a caption naming the creature and round. Mark the chosen row with text ("Chosen") as well as styling. Score terms show sign and units ("+2.1 expected damage"). Rule links are buttons that open the rule text in the right panel and move focus to it. When the setting is off, render nothing and import nothing.
- Motion: respect `prefers-reduced-motion` and the in-app setting everywhere, not just in the replay viewer.
- Copy: plain, short, sentence case. Numbers show units ("12.4 rounds", "68% win rate (±1.8%)").
- Layout works down to 360 px wide; the replay viewer is optimized for laptop screens.
- Charts use LayerChart. Check the LayerChart 2 docs for Svelte 5 usage before writing chart code.
